{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And Elohim heard their groaning.</b> And the prayer of some of them — the righteous of that generation, who prayed then — as it says: וַנִּצְעַק אֶל ה', וַיִּשְׁמַע קוֹלֵנוּ (Deuteronomy 26:7)." "<b>And Elohim remembered His covenant.</b> That He said: וַהֲקִימֹתִי אֶת בְּרִיתִי בֵּינִי וּבֵינֶךָ, וּבֵין זַרְעֲךָ אַחֲרֶיךָ, לִהְיוֹת לְךָ לֵאלֹהִים וּלְזַרְעֲךָ אַחֲרֶיךָ (Genesis 17:7) — and this shall be done whenever we call to Him, as He testified afterward, saying: וְגַם אֲנִי שָׁמַעְתִּי אֶת נַאֲקַת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וגו' וָאֶזְכֹּר אֶת בְּרִיתִי (Exodus 6:5)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:07.910533275Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}